      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HUMZA BEY (2) was heavily-backed and justified the support when resuming last start over 1200m at Sandown-Lakeside, scoring by 1.3 lengths. Fitter for that last hitout and this looks the ideal progression. DOLLAR SHOT (4) was in the money two starts back at Mornington but couldn't back it up last time when tenth, beaten 3 lengths, at Caulfield over 1100m. Tackling a more suitable race this time so she can find the winners' list. THINXZO (3) settled towards the back of the field last start and made little impact in the straight when eighth, beaten 6 lengths, in the race won by HUMZA BEY. Better than that, as the previous two starts suggests. UNTAPPED (6) rediscovered winning form at the first run for a new camp, so maybe they've found the key to him.",
